<Page title="Terms · BeerMat" description="The terms for using BeerMat, BeerMat Pro and BeerMat Online.">
	<article class="wrap prose max-w-3xl py-10">
		<p class="eyebrow">Last updated {updated}</p>
		<h1 class="text-4xl">Terms of use</h1>
		<p>These terms cover the BeerMat desktop app, the BeerMat phone app, BeerMat Online and this website. BeerMat is provided by <strong>Daniel Weatherall, trading as BeerMat, Flat Above, 5 Albert Street, Derby DE1 2DS</strong> (“we”). Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</p>

		<h2>Using BeerMat</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Playing a quiz is free and needs no account.</li>
			<li>BeerMat Free lets you make, save and rehearse quizzes with no limit on questions or rounds: simulated teams play them, and real phones can join a rehearsal to test the connection but can’t play. Hosting a live quiz with real teams playing needs BeerMat Pro.</li>
			<li>Don’t try to break, overload or get round the limits of BeerMat or BeerMat Online, or use them for anything unlawful.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>BeerMat Pro</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>BeerMat Pro is a subscription for a venue, £19.99 a month or £199 a year, paid by card through <strong>Stripe</strong>, which handles billing and receipts.</li>
			<li>It renews automatically at the end of each month or year until you cancel. Cancel any time from the quiz desk (Venue → Manage subscription) or by emailing us; Pro then lasts until the end of the period you’ve paid for, and isn’t charged again.</li>
			<li>You can switch between monthly and yearly in the same place; Stripe adjusts the charge for the time left.</li>
			<li>While a venue has Pro, it’s listed on the BeerMat map and in quiz listings once we’ve checked it’s a real venue. We may decline or remove a listing that’s misleading.</li>
			<li>A licence on the venue’s laptop keeps Pro working offline. If a subscription ends, the laptop returns to BeerMat Free after a short grace period. Your quizzes, questions and results stay on the laptop.</li>
			<li>Refunds: we don’t refund part months or part years. When you cancel, you keep Pro until the end of the period you’ve paid for. If you were charged by mistake (for example twice), email us and we’ll put it right. This doesn’t affect your legal rights.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Your quizzes and music</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Your questions, pictures, sounds and results are yours, and stay on your laptop unless you choose to share them.</li>
			<li>You’re responsible for having the right to use what you put in a quiz, and for the music licences your venue needs to play music in public (in the UK, usually from PPL PRS).</li>
			<li>Venues are responsible for the accuracy of their venue page and quiz nights.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>The shared buzzer library</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Venues on BeerMat Pro can share short sound clips with other BeerMat venues, and add clips others have shared. Anyone using BeerMat can see the names of the clips in the library.</li>
			<li>Clips are chosen and shared by venues, not by us, and appear straight away: we don’t check them first.</li>
			<li>By sharing a clip you confirm that you made it or have permission to share it this way, and that it isn’t offensive or unlawful. You let us store it and let other BeerMat venues copy it and play it at their quizzes; you can take it out of the library at any time (copies venues have already added stay on their laptops).</li>
			<li>A venue that adds a clip is responsible for playing it in public, as with any sound in its quiz.</li>
			<li>To report a clip, use Report in the quiz desk, or email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. If you own the copyright in something shared without your permission, email us the clip’s name and what it’s copied from, and we’ll remove it promptly. A clip reported by three venues is hidden until we’ve looked at it.</li>
			<li>We may remove any clip. We stop venues that repeatedly share clips they have no right to from sharing, and remove the clips they shared.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Accounts</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Keep your password to yourself. You can delete your account at any time in the app.</li>
			<li>We may remove names, pictures or venue pages that are offensive or misleading, and close accounts that break these terms.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Reports, complaints and appeals</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Reporting something:</strong> use Report on a venue’s page in the app, or on a shared buzzer in the quiz desk. For anything else, including a player’s name or picture, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> and tell us what it is and where you saw it.</li>
			<li><strong>What we do:</strong> we look at every report, usually within a few days. Anything illegal comes down as soon as we know about it; anything else that breaks these terms comes down too. If you emailed us, we’ll reply to say what we did.</li>
			<li><strong>Appeals:</strong> if we removed something of yours, hid a buzzer you shared, or closed or limited your account, and you think we got it wrong, email us within 28 days saying what it was and why. We’ll look at it again and reply within 14 days, and put it back if we were wrong.</li>
			<li><strong>Complaints:</strong> if you’re unhappy with how we handled a report, or with how we keep BeerMat safe, email us and we’ll reply within 14 days. You can also tell <a href="https://www.ofcom.org.uk/online-safety">Ofcom</a>, which regulates online safety in the UK (it doesn’t deal with individual complaints, but uses them in its work).</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Our responsibility</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>We work hard to keep BeerMat reliable, but we can’t promise BeerMat Online will always be available. Quizzes themselves run on your laptop and don’t depend on it.</li>
			<li>Nothing in these terms limits liability that can’t be limited by law, including for death or personal injury caused by negligence, or your rights as a consumer.</li>
			<li>Otherwise, for business customers our total liability is limited to what you paid us in the 12 months before the claim, and we aren’t liable for lost profits or business.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Changes and law</h2>
		<p>We may update these terms; if a change matters, we’ll tell Pro customers by email before it takes effect. These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales.</p>
	</article>
</Page>
